# Entity search combobox (system entities & dictionaries)

**Gate:** list/detail/form context is governed by **`.cursor/rules/backend-views-conventions.mdc`**.

Use **`EntitySearchCombobox`** from `@open-mercato/ui/backend/inputs/EntitySearchCombobox` when the user picks a value from a **searchable catalog** — not a short static `<select>`.

**Related:** `.cursor/rules/form-ui-consistency.mdc` (Crud parity, detail grids, `muted` inline editors, `+` in new tab); `.cursor/rules/detail-two-column-layout.mdc` (7fr/3fr detail shell).

**Scope:** Use the same rules for **core** backend pages (`packages/core/src/modules/**/backend/**`) and app modules. Any **FK / association** field that points at another tenant-scoped record (customer entity, user, sales document, resource, supplier row on another entity, etc.) should use **search-backed** pickers (`EntitySearchCombobox` with `onRemoteSearch` when the list is API-driven), not raw UUID `<input>` or unfiltered native `<select>` over large sets.

## CRM: `customerEntityId` (osoba + firma)

- **Wyszukiwanie:** użyj **`remoteSearchCustomerEntities`** (łączy wyniki people + companies) z **`procurementEntitySearch`**, zamiast tylko `/api/customers/companies`.
- **Merge bieżącej wartości:** **`mergeEntitySearchOption`** w edycji inline / gdy etykieta pochodzi z osobnego ładowania.
- **Etykieta (tylko ID):** **`resolveCustomerEntityDisplayLabel`**.
- **Preview + link (szczegóły, sidebar):** **`fetchProcurementCustomerAssociationPreview`** — zwraca `title` / `subtitle` / `recordHref` (osoba → people-v2, firma → companies-v2); nie hard-koduj `/backend/customers/companies/{id}` dla dowolnego UUID.
- **Wzorcowe strony:** create procesu zaopatrzenia; szczegóły procesu (relacja „Customer”); moduł **cases** (create + zakładka Details).

## When to use

1. **System / CRM entities** linked by ID (insurers, partner companies/people, products, etc.) when:
   - the list is large or **server-driven search** is required, or
   - the same pattern is used elsewhere for that relation (stay consistent).
2. **Dictionary-backed fields** (status, type, channel, …) when dictionary entries expose **label** plus optional **`icon`** and **`color`** — the combobox renders the same visual language as elsewhere in the app (chip in list, trigger row).

**Prefer a plain Crud `select`** (without `useEntitySearchCombobox`) only for **small, static** option sets with **no** dictionary appearance and **no** remote search.

## Option shape

Build **`EntitySearchComboboxOption`**: `value`, `label`, optional `description`, and for dictionaries **`icon`**, **`color`** (see `loadInsurerStatusSelectOptions` / dictionary loaders). Merge the **current value** into options when editing legacy/inactive rows so the trigger can resolve the label.

## Trigger appearance (forms + inline edit)

- The combobox **trigger** uses **`Button variant="ghost"`** with **`border border-input`**, **`bg-transparent`**, and a light **`hover:bg-muted/30`** so it matches **Crud-height** controls and **`Inline*Editor`** **`muted`** **`bg-background`** tiles — avoid **`variant="outline"`**’s solid **`bg-background`** on the trigger, which reads as a different “patch” next to plain inputs.

## CrudForm (`select`)

- Set **`useEntitySearchCombobox: true`**.
- Use **`remoteSelectSearch: true`** and **`loadOptions`** that accept a **search string** when the API is query-driven; otherwise load once and rely on local cmdk filter.
- Optional **`createInNewTabHref`** / **`createInNewTabAriaLabel`** for the square `+` (opens `noopener,noreferrer` tab).
- Reuse **`useEntitySearchCombobox` hook** from CrudForm when wiring custom field components.

## Detail pages — preview (read-only)

- Show the same **icon + color + label** as in the combobox list when the field is dictionary-backed: e.g. small icon + colored dot/badge + text in **`renderDisplay`** (or a shared dictionary display helper).
- For entity FKs, show **title + optional subtitle** and links to the target entity when product rules allow.

## Detail pages — inline edit

- Use **`DetailFieldsSection`** / **`InlineSelectEditor`** with **`renderEditor`** that renders **`EntitySearchCombobox`** (same `options` / **`onRemoteSearch`** contract as on the create form).
- Persist via the same **`onSave`** / patch API as other inline fields; keep **`merge*OptionIfMissing`** so the current ID always resolves when opening the editor.

## Do not

- Use a native `<select>` for **dictionary-with-appearance** or **search-backed entity** pickers in new UI — it drifts from platform patterns and loses icon/color/search.
- Duplicate bespoke Popover+cmdk pickers; extend **`EntitySearchCombobox`** or shared helpers instead.
